course: dictionary
lesson: 11603
title: Applicability: where a rule fits
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Applicability is a noun. It comes from the word applicable, and it means how far something can be used for, or fits, a particular case or situation. When you ask about applicability, you are asking: does this apply here?
explain: «The rule about washing hands has general applicability.» General means for many situations, so this rule can be used in the kitchen, the classroom and the park. A rule with wide applicability works in lots of places.
explain: «We checked the applicability of the rule to our science test.» Here the question is whether the rule fits this test. If it fits, the rule has applicability; if it does not, it has none.
explain: The phrase applicability to names what the rule fits. «Its applicability to maths problems is clear.» To test it, put the rule into the situation and see if it works. If it does, it applies.
fact: Applicability means how far something can be used for, or fits, a particular case or situation.
fact: Applicability is a noun, and applicable is the word it comes from.
fact: «General applicability» means a rule can be used in many different situations.
fact: To check applicability, ask: does this rule fit this kind of problem?
fact: Applicability is used in science, maths and law.
exercise: «The rule about washing hands has general applicability.» What does general applicability mean? | It is very loud | *It can be used in many different situations | It is written in red | It is only used on Sundays
exercise: «We checked the applicability of the rule to our problem.» What was being checked? | The colour of the rule | *Whether the rule fits our problem | The name of the teacher
exercise: Which question asks about applicability? | How many pages are in the book? | What is your favourite colour? | *Does this rule fit this kind of problem?
test: Which is the best meaning of applicability? | A kind of bird | *How far something can be used for or fits a case | A sort of cake | The speed of a car
test: «The rule has wide applicability, so it works in many places.» Wide applicability means? | It is only in one room | It is very heavy | *It works in many places | It is hard to read
exam: «Does this rule have any applicability to a cake recipe?» What does this question ask? | How many eggs are needed | *Whether the rule can be used for the recipe | The name of the cook | The colour of the recipe
